course: dictionary
lesson: 14635
title: Formal words that mean possible
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Practicable is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in school rules, official letters and plans. It means something can be done in real life, so it is realistic and can work.
explain: «The school will mend the gate as soon as practicable.» The clue is «as soon as», so practicable must mean as soon as it can be done. Check by swapping in your meaning: «as soon as it can be done» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Teachers and rules often say «where practicable», which means where it is possible. Keep an eye out for this phrase, because it appears in many official documents.
fact: Practicable means able to be done or put into practice successfully.
fact: Practicable means possible in real life, not just in a dream.
fact: Practicable is an adjective, so it describes a plan, an idea or a way of doing something.
fact: «As soon as practicable» means as soon as it can be done.
fact: «Where practicable» means where it is possible.
exercise: «The teacher said the trip would go ahead if it was practicable.» What does practicable mean here? | *Able to be done in real life | Full of loud noise | Impossible to even imagine | Very long and tiring
exercise: «The bus company will change the route where practicable.» What does where practicable mean? | *where it is possible | where it is far away | where it is loud | where it is free
exercise: Which plan is practicable for one class with one lunch break? | A plan to fly the whole class to the moon | *A plan to tidy the library in one lunch break | A plan to turn the playground into the sea | A plan to make the sun shine at night
test: «We will reply as soon as practicable.» What does as soon as practicable mean? | as soon as the clock strikes twelve | *as soon as it can be done | only on Sundays | never, not at all
test: Which word is closest in meaning to practicable? | enormous | silly | *possible | doubtful
exam: Which sentence uses practicable correctly? | The dragon was practicable and flew over the school | Practicable is the colour of the sky on a sunny day | I practicable my spelling every night by the sea | *The club will change the meeting time where practicable, so everyone can attend
